“How does telemetry physically/network-wise move from one subscription
resource to another subscription workspace?”

VERY IMPORTANT UNDERSTANDING

Cross-subscription does NOT automatically mean:
VNet peering required
private connectivity required

Usually Azure Monitor traffic goes through:

Azure control plane / Azure Monitor public endpoints

NOT directly VM-to-workspace private IP communication.

What Happens Internally?

AMA agent inside VM:
collects logs
securely sends telemetry over HTTPS
to:
Azure Monitor ingestion endpoints

Azure backend routes data into correct workspace.

NETWORK FLOW
VM
↓
Azure Monitor Agent
↓
HTTPS 443
↓
Azure Monitor Ingestion Endpoint
↓
Workspace


IMPORTANT NETWORKING CONCEPT
Subscription Is NOT Network Boundary

This is VERY important.

People confuse:

Subscription

with:

Network isolation

They are different.

Subscription = Management/Billing Boundary

NOT network boundary.

Networking Actually Controlled By
VNet
NSG
Firewall
UDR
Private Endpoint
DNS
So Cross-Subscription Telemetry Works Because

Azure Monitor service is global Azure-managed platform service.

As long as:
authentication valid
RBAC valid
outbound connectivity exists

logs can flow.
ENTERPRISE NETWORKING ARCHITECTURE

Very commonly:

Spoke Subscription A
Spoke Subscription B
Spoke Subscription C
         ↓
Hub Network
         ↓
Central Monitoring

But Telemetry Usually Still Uses Azure Monitor Endpoints

NOT direct workspace IP communication.

HOW SECURITY WORKS?

AMA authenticates using:

Managed Identity
OR
Azure AD tokens

Then Azure validates:

DCR permissions
workspace permissions

before accepting logs.

IMPORTANT ENTERPRISE SECURITY TOPICS
1. Private Link / Azure Monitor Private Link Scope (AMPLS)

Large enterprises may NOT allow public internet telemetry.

Then they use:

Azure Monitor Private Link Scope

This enables:

private telemetry ingestion

through private endpoints.

Architecture
VM
↓
Private Endpoint
↓
Azure Monitor Private Link
↓
Workspace

